{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785098715,"nonce":"mmaYdzh2a1y8PDUvvsrBjreeBCw=","title":"ADR-0061 s3-feed replaced `DebugLauncher::launch_debug`'s copy-pasted control-plane","message":"feed (git-bug 64897db, now closed) with the same `scarab-wsfetch` init container a\nreal Step uses, plus a `debug`-attempt workspace token in a per-Pod Secret.\n\nThe code compiles, the shared container builder is unit-tested through\n`build_pod`'s tests, and the real Step path is proven live. **The debug Pod path\nitself is not**: reaching it needs the UI's \"open a shell on this step\" affordance\n(or a direct `DebugLauncher` call) against a finished Run with a snapshot, which\nnothing in the automated tiers does.\n\nSpecifically unverified:\n\n1. that the `debug`-attempt token verifies at the service — it is minted with\n   `attempt: \"debug\"` and a single root, so the codec and the roots check are\n   exercised on a fence that no Step ever produces;\n2. that `expiry_for(now, ttl_secs)` gives a sensible window for a long-lived debug\n   Pod. `ttl_secs` is a `u64` narrowed with `u32::try_from(...).unwrap_or(u32::MAX)`,\n   and `expiry_for` caps at 24 h — so a debug Pod with a TTL longer than a day\n   outlives its own token. Harmless today (the fetch happens in the first seconds)\n   and wrong if anything later re-reads content;\n3. that the Secret is created before the kubelet gives up mounting it. The Pod is\n   created first so the Secret can be owner-referenced to it — the same order every\n   other per-Pod credential uses, where a FailedMount resolves on the kubelet's\n   retry — but for the debug Pod that ordering has never been observed working.\n\nA live test would need a `DebugLauncher` call in the kind tier with a snapshot from\na prior step, which is a small addition to `tests/cluster.rs`.","files":null}]}